# Best Practices & Standards: VST Plugin Development

## JUCE Framework Best Practices (2025-2026)

### Build System: CMake Over Projucer

| Aspect | CMake (Recommended) | Projucer |
|--------|---------------------|----------|
| Version control | Excellent (text-based) | Poor (GUI-generated) |
| CI/CD integration | Native support | Difficult |
| Cross-platform | Automatic | Manual regeneration |
| IDE support | Better (IntelliSense) | Limited |

**Best Practice:** Use CMake with FetchContent for self-contained builds.

```cmake
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.22)
project(MyPlugin)

include(FetchContent)
FetchContent_Declare(JUCE
    GIT_REPOSITORY https://github.com/juce-framework/JUCE.git
    GIT_TAG juce-8.0.4)

set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17)
add_subdirectory(${JUCE_SOURCE_DIR})
```

### C++ Standard: C++17 or C++20

Modern JUCE projects should use **C++17 minimum** (C++20 preferred):

- `constexpr` and compile-time optimizations
- Structured bindings
- RAII patterns for resource management
- `std::atomic` with proper memory ordering

### Thread-Safe Parameter Management

```cpp
namespace Parameters {
    inline const juce::ParameterID gainParam{"gain", 1};

    inline juce::AudioProcessorValueTreeState::ParameterLayout createLayout() {
        std::vector<std::unique_ptr<juce::RangedAudioParameter>> params;

        params.push_back(std::make_unique<juce::AudioParameterFloat>(
            gainParam, "Gain",
            juce::NormalisableRange<float>(0.0f, 1.0f, 0.01f),
            0.5f));

        return {params.begin(), params.end()};
    }
}
```

### Real-Time Audio Safety

**Never on Audio Thread:**
- `new`/`delete` — use pre-allocation
- `std::mutex::lock()` — use lock-free structures
- `malloc()`/`free()` — use memory pools
- File I/O — use background threads
- System calls — avoid entirely
- Virtual function first calls — warm up in prepareToPlay()

**Best Pattern:**
```cpp
void prepareToPlay(double sampleRate, int samplesPerBlock) override {
    // ✅ Pre-allocate all buffers
    workBuffer.setSize(2, samplesPerBlock);

    // ✅ Initialize DSP state
    filter.prepare({sampleRate, (juce::uint32)samplesPerBlock, 2});
    filter.reset();

    // ✅ Warm up virtual calls
    filter.processSample(0.0f);
}
```

### Memory Ordering

Use `acquire/release` for efficient one-way data transfer:

```cpp
// UI Thread
void updateGain(float newGain) {
    gain.store(newGain, std::memory_order_release);
}

// Audio Thread
float processAudio() {
    return gain.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
}
```

