## Sound Design Standards

### Synthesis Type Taxonomy

| Type | Core Mechanism | Best For |
|------|---------------|----------|
| **Subtractive** | Rich oscillators + filters | Classic analog sounds |
| **FM** | Operator modulation | Bells, metallic, electric pianos |
| **Wavetable** | Morphing between waveforms | Evolving pads, modern basses |
| **Granular** | Grain manipulation | Textures, atmospheres |
| **Additive** | Harmonic summing | Organ-like, precise control |

### Parameter Smoothing

All modulation must be smoothed to prevent clicks:

```cpp
juce::SmoothedValue<float> smoothedCutoff;

void prepareToPlay(double sr, int) {
    smoothedCutoff.reset(sr, 0.02f); // 20ms smoothing
}

void processBlock(juce::AudioBuffer<float>& buffer, juce::MidiBuffer&) {
    for (int channel = 0; channel < buffer.getNumChannels(); ++channel) {
        for (int sample = 0; sample < buffer.getNumSamples(); ++sample) {
            float cutoff = smoothedCutoff.getNextValue();
            // Use smoothed value
        }
    }
}
```

## UI/UX Standards

### Control Selection

| Control Type | Best For | Considerations |
|--------------|----------|---------------|
| **Knobs** | Space-efficient, familiar | Awkward mouse interaction |
| **Sliders** | Level comparison, intuitive | Limited by length resolution |
| **Gauges** | Hybrid benefits | Requires user learning |

### Accessibility Requirements

- Minimum 44x44px touch targets
- Full keyboard support (arrows, Page Up/Down, Home/End)
- ARIA labels for screen readers
- High-contrast mode support

### Visual Standards

- Dark theme dominant in audio software
- Group related controls logically
- Visual hierarchy through spacing
- Clear feedback on interaction

